<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vredenburg</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1529–1577</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vredenburg was a castle built by Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a> in the city of Utrecht from 1529, after he acquired the secular lordship of the prince-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> in 1528. Intended to control the citizens, it was besieged and demolished by them in 1577 during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch-revolt">Dutch Revolt</a>. Its remains lie beneath the present Vredenburg square.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vredenburg.jpg" alt="Vredenburg" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Morné van Rooyen · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vredenburg.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
